# Nucleus HUD Walkthrough

## Overview
This document tracks the verification and usage of the Nucleus HUD features.

## Mission 1: System Health (Completed)
- **Status**: ✅ Verified
- **Feature**: Real-time system status indicator.
- **Verification**: Browser test confirmed "System Normal" and Green pulse.

## Mission 2: Research Interface (Completed)
- **Status**: ✅ Verified
- **Feature**: Dispatch research missions via WebOps.
- **Verification**: Browser test dispatched "Browser Test Mission" and received confirmation.

## Mission 3: Neural Link (Completed)
- **Status**: ✅ Verified
- **Feature**: Chat interface with the Brain.
- **Verification**: Browser test sent "Hello" and received "UPLINK SUCCESSFUL".

## Mission 4: The Voice of Nucleus (Verified)
- **Status**: ✅ Verified
- **Feature**: Text-to-Speech (TTS) for system events.
- **Implementation**: [VoiceSynthesizer.tsx](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/tools/nucleus-hud/app/components/VoiceSynthesizer.tsx) hook (Client-side).
- **Verification**: 
    - UI "VOICE ON/OFF" toggle verified (Recording available).
    - Event logic integration confirmed.

## Mission 5: The Eyes of Argus (Verified)
- **Status**: ✅ Verified
- **Feature**: Visual Memory Dashboard ([MemoryMatrix](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/tools/nucleus-hud/app/components/MemoryMatrix.tsx#14-86)).
- **Implementation**: 
    - `/api/memory` endpoint returning file structure (Verified via unit test).
    - [MemoryMatrix.tsx](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/tools/nucleus-hud/app/components/MemoryMatrix.tsx) component visualizing `.brain` nodes.

## Mission 6: Marketing Autopilot (Verified)
- **Status**: ✅ Verified
- **Feature**: Automated marketing loop controlled via HUD.
- **Implementation**:
    - Backend: `/api/autopilot` triggers background thread in [server.py](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/scripts/orchestrator_server.py).
    - Event Stream: Uses [emit_event](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/runtime/event_stream.py#55-93) to write to `events.jsonl` (visible in HUD) and push to Cloud Bridge.
    - Frontend: Toggle "ENABLE AUTOPILOT" -> "AUTOPILOT ENGAGED".
- **Verification**: 
    - Toggle functionality verified in Browser Test.
    - Event emission logic refactored to ensure local file visibility.

